    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Four-bedroom (one ensuite) traditional cottage originally built in 1888, which has been extensively renovated and extended in recent years. This charming home enjoys spectacular views over Lough Keel and the surrounding Donegal countryside.\n\nLough Keel Cottage is a highly unique property, set in the peaceful rural landscape of Carrownasaul, Termon. The property enjoys a wonderful, elevated outlook, with beautiful views across Lough Keel and a picturesque rural landscape, creating a truly scenic setting.\n\nThe accommodation comprises of a living room, kitchen-dining area, four bedrooms, one of which has an ensuite and walk-in wardrobe, and two bathrooms, offering generous space for family living, a permanent home or a peaceful countryside retreat. The property also benefits from ample parking to both the front and side, providing additional convenience.\n\nOne of the property`s most appealing features is its location. Surrounded by the natural beauty of the Donegal landscape, the views over Lough Keel provide an ever-changing backdrop throughout the seasons. The tranquil setting offers the opportunity to enjoy the peace and privacy of rural living while remaining within easy reach of the local community and amenities in the nearby Termon village, with Letterkenny being easily accessible also.\n\nDating back to 1888, Lough Keel Cottage has a distinctive history and character, while its four-bedroom layout provides the space required for modern family living. This represents an exceptional opportunity to acquire a home in a beautiful part of Donegal, with stunning lake views, countryside surroundings and a unique history dating back over 130 years.\n\n---\n\nConcrete steps lead to a partially glazed, hardwood front door.\n\nEntrance Hallway: 9.1 x 6.9 ft, with tiled flooring.\n\nLiving Room: 12.7 x 13.6 ft, with timber flooring and recessed lighting. Features a solid fuel stove with a back boiler, set on a tiled plinth. This room overlooks beautiful views of Lough Keel and the surrounding countryside. \n\nKitchen-Dining Room: 12.8 x 14 ft, with tiled flooring and recessed lighting. Built-in wall and base kitchen units, with a stainless-steel double sink and drainer unit, with mixer taps over. Integrated four-ring electric hob and integrated electric oven, with a built-in extractor hood over, and plumbed for dishwasher. With beautiful views extending across Lough Keel and the surrounding countryside, this room is a particularly scenic space.\n\nBedroom One: 11.7 x 11.1 ft, with timber flooring, and enjoying a wonderful outlook. Walk-in wardrobe with extensive shelving and hanging space, with timber flooring and recessed lighting.\nEnsuite: Tiled flooring and fully tiled walls. A white three-piece suite, with a Triton T90 electric shower over the bath.\n\nBedroom Two: 12.5 x 11.3 ft, with carpet flooring and recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom Three: 15.1 x 8.2 ft, with carpet flooring and recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom Four: 15.1 x 8.6 ft, with carpet flooring and recessed lighting.\n\nRear Hallway: A partially glazed PVC door leads to the rear.\n\nShower Room: Tiled flooring and fully tiled walls, with a storage cabinet beneath the wash hand basin. A white two-piece suite, and separate shower cubicle with glass shower enclosure, containing a Triton T90 electric shower. \n\nOutside: Extensive gravelled area to the front, providing ample parking, in addition to parking space to the side. The front garden is laid to lawn, while the property overlooks fabulous countryside views.\n\nDisclaimer - The above particulars are issued by Glen Estates on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through them. Information contained in the brochure does not form any part of any offer or contract and is provided in good faith, for guidance only. Glen estates have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. Maps and plans are not to scale and measurements are approximate, photographs provided for guidance only. The particulars, descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, permissions or licences for use or occupation, access and any other details, such as prices, rents or any other outgoings are for guidance only and may be subject to change. Intending purchasers / tenants must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of details provided to them either verbally or as part of this brochure. Neither Glen Estates or any of its employees have any authority to make or give any representation or warranty in respect of this property.\n"
      },
